
<p>Miriam Pawel, in an op-ed in The New York Times arguing that University of California should not bring back the SAT requirement for admission:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>What has made the University of California exceptional is its
commitment to increase access without sacrificing excellence.
[...] Students on University of California campuses may struggle
with basic math, but they are graduating at record rates.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>A success story would be increasing the number of people with solid math skills. Printing degrees for students who struggle with basic math is not a success story, and sounds like the antithesis of “academic excellence”.</p>

